-- Two shooters: one firing every 10 frames at a normal speed (so the shot is still
-- alive at frame 6), one firing every frame at speed 40 (so its shots leave the world
-- and get culled). The game draws whatever is in `shots`, so per-frame parity covers
-- spawning, motion, aiming and culling.
player is {x: 20, y: 60}
turret is {x: 100, y: 60}
fast is {x: 60, y: 100}
turret shoots at player every 10 frames speed 2
fast shoots at player every 1 frames speed 40
to update
  player.x is player.x + 1
to draw
  clear screen to black
  draw rect at player.x, player.y size 6, 6 in white
  draw rect at turret.x, turret.y size 6, 6 in red
  each sh in turret.shots
    draw rect at sh.x, sh.y size 2, 2 in yellow
  draw rect at fast.x, fast.y size 6, 6 in cyan
  each sh in fast.shots
    draw rect at sh.x, sh.y size 2, 2 in orange
run game with update and draw
